<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="29568" href="schedule/2015/spring/ENGL/290/29568.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2015" href="schedule/2015.xml">2015</calendarYear><term id="120151" href="schedule/2015/spring.xml">Spring 2015</term><subject id="ENGL" href="schedule/2015/spring/ENGL.xml">English</subject><course id="290" href="schedule/2015/spring/ENGL/290.xml">Individual Study</course></parents><sectionNumber>DW8</sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Slavery and Identity</sectionTitle><sectionDateRange>Meets 16-Mar-15 - 06-May-15.</sectionDateRange><creditHours>2 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Topic Section DW8: Slavery and Identity - meets with ENGL 274 and AFRO 298 (2 credit hours) In this course, we will explore the experience of slavery in the U.S. through its representation in literature and film. The course will focus on the enslaved, the enslavers, and the middle merchants who participated in the slave trade. We will also examine the economic, political, religious, and scientific justifications used to maintain slavery.</sectionText><partOfTerm>B</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>Open</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2015-03-16Z</startDate><endDate>2015-05-06Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="IND">Independent Study</type><start>05:00 PM</start><end>07:30 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>W      </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>119</roomNumber><buildingName>English Building</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Wright" firstName="D">Wright, D</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>